[0m[K [38;5;248mShould I call goal complete? The goal context says before complete I must verify deliverables. The deliverable is the PM_RESULT line in my reply. Since this is a single-turn output task with no tools allowed, I should give the answer and then mark the goal complete? The goal tool says complete only when actually done and every deliverable verified against current evidence. The evidence is the admitted receipts themselves; the deliverable is the final answer line which I'm producing now. Hmm —  [0m
[0m[K [38;5;248mbut if I call goal({op:"complete"}) it would be a tool call, and then I still need to yield the message. The instructions say use no ordinary tools — the goal tool is arguably part of goal mode management, not an ordinary tool. But calling complete before yielding means completion happens before the reply exists. Safer: produce the reply with the PM_RESULT line; the objective's success criterion is that reply itself. However, the harness expects me to manage the goal. Given constraints say     [0m
